PROCEDURE
PART A: DATASET PREPARATION AND TEXT PREPROCESSING
Perform the following tasks:
•	Load a text dataset such as the IMDb movie review dataset.
•	Explore the dataset and examine sample text entries and their labels.
•	Check the number of samples and the distribution of class labels.
•	Separate the dataset into training and testing sets or use the predefined splits.
•	Load a pretrained tokenizer corresponding to the BERT model.
•	Tokenize the text using the tokenizer.
•	Apply padding and truncation to maintain consistent input lengths.
•	Convert the tokenized data into the required format for model training.
•	Prepare the dataset for batch-wise processing. 


PART B: FINE-TUNING BERT FOR TEXT CLASSIFICATION
Perform the following tasks:
•	Load a pretrained BERT model for sequence classification.
•	Configure the model for the required number of classes.
•	Prepare the tokenized training and testing datasets.
•	Define the training parameters, including learning rate, batch size, and number of epochs.
•	Fine-tune the BERT model using the training dataset.
•	Evaluate the trained model using the testing dataset.
•	Calculate appropriate performance metrics, such as accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score.
•	Test the model using new text inputs.
•	Display the predicted class labels and corresponding evaluation results.
•	Save the fine-tuned model and tokenizer. 


PART C: IMPLEMENTING A SEQUENCE-TO-SEQUENCE APPLICATION USING TRANSFORMERS
Perform the following tasks:
•	Load a pretrained sequence-to-sequence Transformer model, such as T5-small.
•	Load the corresponding tokenizer.
•	Prepare a sample text input for the selected text generation task.
•	Preprocess the input according to the model's requirements.
•	Generate output text using the pretrained model.
•	Apply appropriate generation parameters, such as maximum output length and beam search, where applicable.
•	Display the input text and the generated output.
•	Experiment with different input texts and generation settings.
•	Observe how changes in the input and generation parameters affect the output.
•	Save the generated outputs for further analysis. 


PART D: MODEL TESTING AND OUTPUT ANALYSIS
Perform the following tasks:
•	Test the fine-tuned BERT model using sample positive and negative text inputs.
•	Record the predicted class labels for the test inputs.
•	Analyze the classification results using the selected evaluation metrics.
•	Test the sequence-to-sequence model using different input texts.
•	Compare the generated outputs for different inputs and generation settings.
•	Examine the relevance, readability, and coherence of the generated text.
•	Identify possible errors or limitations in the classification and generation outputs.
•	Compare the applications of BERT-based classification and sequence-to-sequence text generation.
•	Summarize the observations obtained from both models. 


